  "scope": "The exact unfiltered collective density response has a spectral-edge term that forces its first-harmonic gradient coefficient to grow with radius. Its flat counterpart has an anisotropic |p| cusp. A new polynomial taper in the interaction removes that obstruction in this channel, preserves the free determinant, and retains a finite-species nonlinear enclosure. The recomputed homogeneous Gaussian curvature coefficient has the Einstein sign in a finite coupling range but changes sign at sufficiently strong coupling. Full observable locality, fixed-eight-species Einstein dynamics, microscopic refinement, Lorentzian gravity, Standard Model and TOE remain unproved. No new Lean theorem."
